=== P2d: the SAME concurrent commit, at EVERY point of the snapshot, never produces a mixed view ===
OK   the snapshot issues a fixed, small set of statements (candidates, occurrences, preferences, habit logs, availability flag, availability periods, plans) -- 7 here
[info] k=0:S1 k=1:S0 k=2:S0 k=3:S0 k=4:S0 k=5:S0 k=6:S0 k=7:S0
OK   COHERENT AT EVERY COMMIT POINT: a concurrent commit after the 1st .. 7th statement (after the snapshot exists) is invisible to the WHOLE evaluation -- both candidates' evidence is deeply equal to S0; a commit before the first statement (the snapshot not yet taken) is seen by ALL of it -- deeply equal to S1
OK   SAME SNAPSHOT FOR EVERY CANDIDATE: at no commit point does one candidate see the old shared state and another the new one
=== REPEATABLE READ is what is actually emitted, and a later evaluation sees the commit ===
OK   ACTUAL ISOLATION: inside the snapshot `transaction_isolation` is "repeatable read"; a plan committed by another connection AFTER the snapshot exists is NOT visible to the next read of the same transaction (count 0 then 0), and IS visible to a NEW snapshot (1)
OK   CONTROL: under the default isolation (READ COMMITTED) the same second read DOES see the concurrent commit (0 then 1) -- the repeatable-read behavior above is real, not an artifact
OK   NEXT EVALUATION SEES THE COMMIT (no stale cross-request cache): an evaluation started before the commit says S0 for both candidates, and the very next evaluation says S1 for both
=== the snapshot executor: read-only, bounded, and it does not outlive the snapshot ===
OK   READ-ONLY BY CONSTRUCTION: a write statement and a multi-statement text are rejected before reaching the driver, and the executor is unusable once the snapshot has ended (the transaction client never escapes)
=== query bound: constant in the number of candidates; one snapshot per evaluation ===
OK   QUERY BOUND: 2 candidates and 6 candidates cost exactly the same: 7 statements in 1 snapshot (O(1) in the candidate count -- the occurrence read is one batched query, there is no per-candidate transaction or query)
OK   all six candidates of the one evaluation have evidence from the same snapshot (identical shared supply view)
OK   with no recurrence candidate at all the snapshot reads only the candidates, the preferences and the habit logs (3 statements) -- availability and plans are not read when no opportunity evidence can exist
=== no contract change: the preview body and signed tokens are identical to the legacy composition when nothing is concurrent ===
OK   PREVIEW AND TOKEN IDENTITY: the full preview body (constructed day, resolved intents, every signed acceptance token) is byte-identical between the legacy and the P2d composition, and so is each candidate's evidence
OK   the preview carries no snapshot, context, pressure or shadow field
=== the reads mean exactly what they meant: overnight, half-open, lifecycle, duration sources, timezone / DST ===
